"""Mutations of part 8d-i's birds and mesh player (src/game/birds.*, src/game/mesh_player.*) for
../mutfast.py with the world build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_8d1.py --models DIR --build build_world.bat --check check_world.py

DIR holds a .txt per mission ("mission NAME"; the tests run the same in each). Each mutation should
make check_world.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Generated from the 8d-i lines only (a
comparison, a number, an operator or a statement per line), then pruned. Left out as equivalent
(29): the unit tests' sq + 1 (normalizing a vector of square exactly 1 changes nothing); the short
vectors' x != 0.5 / z != 0.5 (a square under 1e-8 has no component near 0.5); the destructor's
nulled model and wings; the level-out's whole short-vector branch (its square is at least 0.01:
dead code) and its unit test against 1.5 or sq + 1 (x and z were normalized: at most 1 + 0.01); the
moved flag after a move (a bird off its seat always flaps, which updates the model anyway); the
initial m_unknown40 and m_timer (the constructor sets both); the mesh player's m_frames.clear() in
Play (Free leaves it empty), m_movie = movie (Load set it before) and the nulled textures (the
vector is cleared after). 6 more did not compile and were dropped (the states' enum values as
floats, an unused header line).

Run 1 (247): 189 caught, 52 survived, 6 not built. New cases for 23: the states' values; a bird's children searched (the callback's 0 goes on into them); seeds whose rand()s reach 20000 (the waits' % 20000 and % 5000); the hop's RandomFloat max; a take-off along z and exactly 10 m up; a level climb (y 0), a climb and a fly-off of square exactly 1.5, short vectors along x, z and y; a level-out with both squares exactly 1 (y -0.1 itself); the glide exactly at the far clip and with the camera off the origin. Run 2 (209): all caught.
"""
